In order to detect the moisture stability of the \(C_{3}\mathrm{N}_{3}\) -modified PSCs, we also tracked PCE of the device under RH of \(60\,\pm\,5\%\) for \(500\,\mathrm{~h~}\) (Figure 5f). Compared with the very low stability of the control device \((26\%)\) , the CN-7.5 device can maintain about \(90\%\) of its initial PCE. This result conclusively indicates that the addition of \(C_{3}\mathrm{N}_{3}\) improves the moisture stability, agreeing with the contact angle (Figure 2f).
## 3. Conclusions
3. ConclusionsIn summary, we have optimized the crystallization and morphology of perovskite for highly efficient and moisture stable planar PSCs employing \( C_{3}\mathrm{N}_{3} \) as an additive. It was revealed that \( C_{3}\mathrm{N}_{3} \) can interact with uncoordinated \( \mathrm{Pb}^{2+} \) and \( \mathrm{MA}^{+} \)so as to reduce the defects and suppress charge recombination. As the consequence, the PSCs constructed with perovskite and \( C_{3}\mathrm{N}_{3} \) achieved an excellent PCE of \( 19.91\% \) with more durable moisture stability. This work demonstrates \( C_{3}\mathrm{N}_{3} \) has a good potential in PSCs and its further applications in other optoelectronic devices may emerge in the near future.
